{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788973058,"nonce":"b4zs5JkN8d1TFJTU+KBco96ZQOE=","message":"IMPLEMENTED, 2026-09-09, on branch `worktree-agent-a3ce8c663c1f66155`\n(`242a123` feat, `4f84e49` Build). Release, pdb path checked, `dotnet build -c\nRelease` clean with 0 warnings. No game was launched;\n`accept/ae84a07-abilities.md` carries the bench acceptance as a numbered\ncommand list and this issue stays open until the orchestrator has run it.\n\n**Shipped**: `abilities {pawn|pawns, target?, cap?}` and `ability-cast\n{pawn|pawns, ability, target?, dest?, queue?}` in a new\n`Source/AutoRimmer/AbilityVerbs.cs` (~1600 lines with the citations), plus two\nguarded routes in `PawnSafe.cs` (`Abilities`, `Baby`) and their Class E / Class\nC header entries, plus a DESIGN decisions-log entry.\n\n\nAll nine corrections and all eleven additions CONFIRMED as written, verbatim,\nby member name. Specifically re-verified because the implementation depends on\nthem: `Ability.CanCast` is an `AcceptanceReport` whose `Psycast` override\nbranches mutually exclusively on `def.EntropyGain \u003e float.Epsilon` (so it is\nnever the gate here, only clause B9); `Ability_PsyfocusCost` /\n`Ability_EntropyGain` are `StatDef`s read through\n`statBases.GetStatValueFromList`; there is no `Ability.ValidateTarget` (only\n`ValidateGlobalTarget`) and `Verb_CastAbility.ValidateTarget` does not call\n`base`; there is no `PsylinkLevel` on the entropy tracker\n(`PawnUtility.GetPsylinkLevel` sums `Hediff_Psylink.level`); it is\n`GetGizmos()`; `Ability.verb` reads the private `verbTracker` field;\n`QueueCastingJob` is void with exactly two overloads; `CompUseEffect_GainAbility`\nis the psytrainer comp and its level check is only `ConfirmMessage`;\n`AllAbilitiesForReading` clears/refills and reassigns in the mutant-whitelist\nbranch; `CanApplyOn` iterates the PRIVATE `effectComps` field while\n`ValidateTarget` gates on `Valid`, so the two are never both called.\n\n**Three corrections to the correction, all small:**\n\n1. **\"18 gizmo-layer refusals\" enumerates 16.** B1–B16 is 5 (`Psycast`) + 11\n   (`Ability`) and that is exactly right. The missing two — three, in fact —\n   are at the VISIBILITY layer, which the comment's addition E rules out of\n   scope by saying the verb must not touch gizmos. It must not *construct* one;\n   the clauses that decide whether one is drawn are still refusals, because a\n   gizmo that is never drawn cannot be clicked. Shipped as V1\n   `not-controlled` (`Pawn_AbilityTracker.GetGizmos`' `IsColonistPlayerControlled\n   || IsColonyMechPlayerControlled || IsColonySubhumanPlayerControlled ||\n   IsColonyAnimal`), V2 `gizmo-hidden` (`(Drafted ||\n   displayGizmoWhileUndrafted) \u0026\u0026 ability.GizmosVisible()` — the second half is\n   false when any effect comp sets `ShouldHideGizmo`), and V3\n   `gizmo-hidden-drafted` (`Ability.GetGizmos`' `!pawn.Drafted ||\n   def.showWhenDrafted`) / `royalty-missing` (`Psycast.GetGizmos` overrides that\n   clause away and yields only on `ModLister.RoyaltyInstalled`). **Nineteen\n   named gizmo-layer gates**, none of them a Gizmo object.\n\n2. **B11's clause has a fourth term the comment omits.** `Ability.GizmoDisabled`\n   is `!pawn.Drafted \u0026\u0026 def.disableGizmoWhileUndrafted \u0026\u0026 pawn.GetCaravan() ==\n   null \u0026\u0026 !DebugSettings.ShowDevGizmos`. The bench runs with devMode on, so\n   dropping the last term would have made the undrafted refusal unreachable on\n   the very bench that has to demonstrate it. Reproduced in full.\n\n3. **Nine target-layer refusals, eleven gates.** E1–E9 is right; two more are\n   needed and are not in the list. `TargetingParameters.CanTarget` is named in\n   the comment (\"Plus, separately, the targeter applies...\") but not numbered,\n   and it is the ONLY clause that answers the acceptance bullet about refusing\n   a cell for `canTargetLocations:false` — shipped as T0 `target-params`. And\n   `Ability.CanApplyOn(target)`, the clause `QueueCastingJob` itself gates on,\n   is discussed at length in addition B but never given a slot — shipped as T10\n   `cannot-apply`, evaluated separately from `Valid` and after `EffectComps` has\n   been touched, so it is not the silent skip.\n\n\n- **The confirmation.** Addition F's ruling followed: `Ability.ConfirmationDialog`\n  is public and only CONSTRUCTS the window, so `ability-cast` reads it, does\n  not show it, publishes the text as `confirmation`, and reproduces the\n  callback body. **The READ does not call it at all** — a modded comp's\n  `ConfirmationDialog` is free to `Find.WindowStack.Add` on its own, and one\n  force-pausing window wedges the run; `abilities` derives the outlook by\n  reflection over `def.confirmationDialogText` and\n  `CompAbilityEffect.ConfirmationDialog` overrides instead.\n- **`nonInterruptingSelfCast` is the one branch that calls the game's method.**\n  `QueueCastingJob`'s second line is `verb.TryStartCastOn(verb.Caster); return;`\n  — BEFORE `ShowCastingConfirmationIfNeeded`, so that branch provably cannot\n  open a window and takes no job at all. Reproducing it would mean calling\n  `TryStartCastOn` ourselves, which addition I forbids; calling\n  `ability.QueueCastingJob` there is going *through* the game rather than\n  around it. `queue:true` on such an ability is refused at\n  `self-cast-cannot-queue` rather than silently dropped (git-bug `bc2250b`'s\n  rule), and the effect is read back from `verb.WarmingUp` / `ability.Casting`\n  since there is no job id to read.\n- **A modded override is disclosed, not guessed at.** `abilities` reports an\n  `overrides` block naming any subclass that overrides `GizmoDisabled`,\n  `CanCast` or `CanApplyOn` beyond `Ability`/`Psycast`, because the read cannot\n  see such a clause without casting. `ability-cast` calls the real\n  `Ability.GizmoDisabled` after its own nineteen and refuses at\n  `gizmo-disabled` if the override says no — so the act is never weaker than\n  the game.\n- **Fog.** A THING target is fog-filtered like every other order target\n  (`WorldSafe.Hidden`, the project's standing rule and the game's own\n  `IgnoreFogged` default). A CELL target is NOT refused for fog and publishes\n  `fogged` instead: the ability targeter has no fog clause for a location, and\n  the only fog test in the whole path (`Ability.ValidAOEAffectedTarget`) refuses\n  fogged THINGS while picking AOE victims.\n- **Both verbs take the plural.** `ability-cast {pawns:[…]}` fires the same\n  ability from several casters at one target with per-pawn accept/reject, and\n  `abilities` answers for several casters at once, per DESIGN's \"the plural\n  form IS the verb\".\n\n\n`AbilityDef.targetWorldCell` — a world-tile ability. `Ability.QueueCastingJob`\nhas a second overload taking a `GlobalTargetInfo`, with a different comp path\n(`CanApplyOn(GlobalTargetInfo)` reads the PROPERTY, so no silent skip), a\ndifferent target check (`ValidateGlobalTarget`, which passes\n`throwMessages:true` and would spray messages), and a caravan branch that calls\n`Activate` directly and takes no job. `ability-cast` refuses it explicitly at\n`world-target-unsupported`, naming the member, in the same disposition\n`attack`'s `queue-unsupported` takes. **Filed as git-bug `9225c8e`** with an\nAcceptance section. Not blocking: no acceptance bullet on this issue needs it.\n\n\nThe acceptance bullets in the body need two amendments the scoping pass already\nidentified and `accept/ae84a07-abilities.md` carries: Bloodbond gives **Tantrum,\nnot murderous rage, to a violence-incapable victim**, and Fingerkill takes the\n**caster's part FIRST and destroys the heart LAST** — the body has that order\nbackwards. And the caster must be **drafted**: all three bench psycasts set\n`displayGizmoWhileUndrafted` without `disableGizmoWhileUndrafted`, whose default\nis true, so undrafted they refuse at the `undrafted` gate. That is a fingerkill\ndefect, not an AutoRimmer one, and this verb reporting it is the acceptance.","files":null}]}